1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:15,707
I am the clerk. Ask me anything about your institution: who runs an office, when an exam must be printed, whether a course outline follows the rules. I read the answer on the institution's own pages, then and there.

2
00:00:16,099 --> 00:00:27,881
I read the institution's public pages when you ask, and I name the page and the date. I remember what I found, and I re-read the page before relying on it, because people change offices.

3
00:00:27,881 --> 00:00:43,538
I can also review a whole document against the institution's rules, a course outline for instance: every rule for the course's level, every date against the calendar and the holidays, and whether the grades add to one hundred.

4
00:00:43,949 --> 00:00:54,059
When the pages do not say, my answer is Unknown, with the nearest thing they do say. A page behind a login I leave to you, and I say where to read it.

5
00:00:54,059 --> 00:01:09,437
I work with other agents: after a course review, the conscience reviews the outline for equity and inclusion, and the scribe redoes it with the fixes. The docent asks me for a thesis's paperwork and deadlines.

6
00:01:09,849 --> 00:01:17,265
A real run, one example among many. An instructor asks when their final exam must be printed this fall.

7
00:01:17,265 --> 00:01:27,971
I quote the rule and the exam period, each with its page, and work out the date. The course's own exam date sits behind a login, so that part is Unknown.

8
00:01:28,349 --> 00:01:39,938
Another example. Asked who runs the equity, diversity and inclusion office, I answer with the name, title and public email, each from a page I opened.

9
00:01:40,349 --> 00:01:57,418
Then a whole course outline. The university has a rule: no test in the last three weeks of classes. This outline puts a quiz there, so I flag it, quoting the rule and its page. A lab report announced too late breaks a second rule.

10
00:01:57,799 --> 00:02:10,313
These are examples, not a list of what I can do. Ask me anything the institution's pages answer: a policy, a deadline, a form, a fee, a room.

11
00:02:10,699 --> 00:02:20,159
To use me, type your question to Claude Code and name me, the clerk. The first line is my verdict: Correct, Fix or Unknown.

12
00:02:20,159 --> 00:02:31,097
My memory holds short facts from your university's pages, each with its page and date; another university gets a memory of its own.
